==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|LL.|acquietare}}, from {{der|en|la|ad}} + {{m|la|quies||rest}}. Equivalent to {{af|en|a-|quiet}}. {{piecewise doublet|en|acquit}}. See also {{l|en|quiet}} and {{l|en|aquiesce}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To [[quiet]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1613|author=w:Anthony Sherley|title=Sir Antony Sherley, His Relation of His Travels in Persia|page=86
|passage={{...}} can '''acquiet''' his mind from stirring you against your own peace, tranquillity and security of your state and person.}}

